0215: GPU keep-warm, texture creation log

A light frame (a menu over a still picture: ~0.5 ms of GPU work) lets the GPU drop its clocks
within half a second (RTX 3090 Ti, nvidia-smi: P0 1995/10501 MHz core/memory -> P3 ~1000/5001 ->
P5/P8 345-450/405-810 MHz); the first frames of the full scene after it then took 30-60 ms
instead of 6 (4K, enhanced lighting) until the clocks came back: a stutter every time the pause
screen or the Game Boy Horror closed. aurora_set_gpu_keep_warm(units) adds filler work after the
frame's own commands: a compute pass streaming through a 64 MiB buffer (one unit = one read pass,
about 0.06 ms at full clocks; at most 400). ALU-only filler kept the core busy, but the driver
still lowered the memory clock (P3) and the scene is bandwidth-bound at 4K. The application sizes
it by feedback from the frame's GPU time (LM: src/recomp/pacing.cpp, docs/INTERPOLATION.md
"Pass 5").

Debug aids for hitch hunting (off unless set): AURORA_TEX_LOG=1 logs every texture Aurora's
texture/render-texture/copy/pass-snapshot/offscreen paths create; AURORA_ENH_TEX_LOG=1 every
enhanced-lighting render target (re)creation.

